<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29362" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŏdĕrātrix</span></b> ,
			īcis, f.
		moderator. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>She who moderates</i> or <i>allays; a
				directress, mistress, governess</i> (mostly Ciceron.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Cist. 2, 2, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That which rules, guides, controls</i>, etc.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">temperantia est moderatrix omnium commotionum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 5, 14, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">materiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					N. D. 3, 39, 92</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">factorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Phil. 5, 18, 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">officii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Fl. 24, 57</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
